## History — there are NO old copies in this tree; ask the tool
What you see here is the ONE current version. Every prior version is sealed inside
`.handoff/` and is read only through the `handoff` binary — never by browsing it.

    handoff history [PATH]              versions that changed PATH (file or dir), newest first — JSON
    handoff show PATH --at v2           one file exactly as it was at v2
    handoff diff PATH                   what the latest version changed in PATH (unified diff)
    handoff extract PATH DEST --at v2   pull a file / dir / "." out of any version, standalone
    handoff status                      what you have changed since the latest version

If `.handoff/bin/` exists, the binary for your platform is there; otherwise it ships
with the agent-handoff plugin. `handoff verify` proves the store is intact.

## Handing back
When your unit is done: `handoff commit -m "<what changed and why>"` — the comment is
mandatory — then `handoff pack --out <name>.tar.gz`. Pack refuses a tree with
uncommitted changes, so the package's history always matches its contents.
